      "dcDescription": [
        "1921.04.0038 War and head hunting sword from the Dusun people of North Borneo (Sabah and Brunei). Thew sheath with a square carved panel on its upper part combined with the lotus (headhunting) motif, a beaded carrying belt and tufts ofd hair. The antler hilt has hidden human body limbs (an alternative interpretation is leaches) and aso (dragon dog) jaws but no visible human full body sitting figure. The fine blade with several studs and scroll motifs on both sides. Indonesia Malaysia Brunei Inventering av indonesiska vapen Svärd med fäste av vitt ben, med utskärningar samt tofsar av rött och v"
      ],
